; status: works — the waterbomb base [hull2020, ch. 5]. Both diagonals and both
; center lines meet at the square's center; the 8 rays there need |M-V|=2
; (Maekawa) to be realizable. tests/test_collapse.ml empirically verified the
; contiguous 5-valley/3-mountain pattern below (corners + one edge-midpoint
; ray valley, the other three edge-midpoint rays mountain) folds to a UNIQUE
; layer order — no `over` needed.

paper square

mark --ac = map .b onto .d     ; diagonal a-c
mark --bd = map .a onto .c     ; diagonal b-d
mark --h  = map .a onto .d     ; horizontal midline, y = 1/2
mark --v  = map .a onto .b     ; vertical midline, x = 1/2

; the emitted FOLD folded-frame edges_assignment is the derived global-frame
; M/V of the folded state (spec §4.6, multi-crease rule): each ray's letter
; reads off the finished layer order. Here derived = declared for all eight
; rays — no prior flip, so nothing inverts. (The old evaluator's fan-index
; parity adjustment inverted the four midline rays — the .b.c ray valley
; showed M, the other three mountains showed V; that was a bug, fixed by
; the 3D rewrite.)
flatten (--ac & .a) (--ac & .c) (--bd & .b) (--bd & .d)
  (--h & --bc)
  (--h & --da mountain)
  (--v & --cd mountain)
  (--v & --ab mountain)
